E15-S3|E15|Green build deploys to ECS automatically with a tested rollback|build|E15-S2,E15-S4|in_progress|||||||The auto-deploy half is proven and the ROLLBACK HALF IS NOW PROVEN FOR REAL, by accident, on 29 Oct. Build 02860232 registered api:22, worker:22 and portal:20 and updated all three services. api:22 crash-looped (ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND for a new lib import missing its .js extension under node ESM), the deployment circuit breaker fired at 06:34:06 with 'tasks failed to start' and ECS rolled the api back to api:21, which kept serving. So the rollback path is verified by an unplanned production event, which is stronger evidence than a staged test. Separately I did execute one deliberate rollback - the same mechanism - when diagnosing, so the clause is met. REMAINING: the runbook entry is not yet written (belongs with E20-S2), and a second pipeline defect this surfaced is now FIXED in buildspec.yml: `aws ecs wait services-stable` returns success after a rollback because a rolled-back service IS stable, so the build reported SUCCEEDED while serving old code. The build now records each registered task-definition ARN and fails when a service's PRIMARY deployment is not that ARN (verified in build 16f3638b, which passed the new check). Status stays in_progress until the runbook entry exists.
