E15-S8|E15|Container Insights replaced by a free task-stop alert path|build|E15-S6|verified|A-cost|feat/E15-S8-alerts|a671f42|evidence/E15-S8-apply.md|2026-10-29T16:07Z|orchestrator|VERIFIED by me on the live stack, not from the child's report. Plan reviewed before applying: 3 add, 1 change, 3 destroy, with NO task definition in the diff, so ignore_changes from E15-S6 held; applied with -var image_tag=6de0209c9dd9 because terraform.tfvars still pins an older tag and applying on the tfvars would have rolled all three services backwards. After apply, read back from AWS: five alarms remain and none is in ECS/ContainerInsights (api-target-5xx, api-unhealthy-hosts, portal-unhealthy-hosts, rds-connections-high, rds-free-storage-low); cluster containerInsights=disabled; rule evia-beta-task-stopped ENABLED with target arn:aws:sns:ap-south-1:562654496378:evia-beta-ops-alerts. End-to-end proof run by me with scripts/verify-e15s8-task-stop-alert.sh: throwaway task a93db3c3e4b245fc856083a42714c756 ran with exit 3, and the alert came back through EventBridge into the ops SQS sink in 49s with source aws.ecs, detail-type ECS Task State Change, lastStatus STOPPED, desiredStatus STOPPED, stopCode EssentialContainerExited, container exit codes [3]. DEFECT FOUND BY RUNNING IT: the first run crashed because the sink still holds CloudWatch alarm notifications from the E15-S6 proof at 03:41Z, whose SNS Message is an alarm document rather than an EventBridge event, and the reader parsed body[Message] unguarded - fixed in this commit (non-JSON, non-dict and detail-less messages are skipped). The child's rehearsal used an empty isolated queue and never met that case. Saving recorded as an ESTIMATE: 108 measured metric streams x 0.30/metric-month = 32.40 plus 3 alarms x 0.10 = 32.70/month (392.40/yr), because Cost Explorer shows 0.00 for the month and there is no invoice to difference. Given up knowingly: Container Insights was the only per-service CPU/memory source; AWS/ECS free metrics would restore that for about 1.20/month.
E16-S9|E16|The therapist can review a client conversation in the portal|build|E16-S3,E17-S4|verified|A-portal|develop|9702907|evidence/E16-S9.md|2026-10-29T07:25Z|orchestrator|VERIFIED LIVE by the orchestrator, closing the in_review state recorded at 53b9860. The blocker was data, not code: beta had zero TherapistClient rows. Seeded one assignment (ananya.rao@okuvu.in to the one client with a real session) plus two synthetic sessions of 8 turns via scripts/seed-client-demo.sql, then walked the story by HTTPS as that therapist with scripts/verify-conversation-flow.py: login via Cognito hosted UI, caseload 200 with 1 client, requestChatAccess returns success, /clients/<id>/conversation returns 200 rendering 10 turns (5 Client / 5 Agent) across 3 sessions with all 3 fixture markers present. ClinicalAccessLog now reads VIEW_CONVERSATION 10, VIEW_NOTES 5, REQUEST_CHAT_ACCESS 1, VIEW_CLIENT_DETAIL 1. PII scan over the exact read window: 78 events (api 56, portal 22, worker 0), zero hits, so the sign-in lines that E16-S11 redacted stay clean. Negative control included: an unassigned therapist sees an empty caseload and 0 leaked markers, so the render is not a missing access check. Evidence section 9 of the file records the fixture, the transcript and two verification-path defects found on the way (ECS 8192-char overrides cap, and this router having no tRPC transformer so batch envelopes reach zod as the wrong shape).
E16-S10|E16|Account deletion removes every record that references the subject|build|E16-S3|verified|A-deletion|develop|53b9860|evidence/E16-S10.md|2026-10-29T06:56Z|orchestrator|Orchestrator verified the database half directly, which the child explicitly could not: querying production in-VPC shows 45 applied migrations and ALL 18 foreign keys to User now confdeltype='c' (CASCADE), i.e. migration 20261029120000_deletion_cascade_on_user is live. Code is live too: api:23 image tag 53b9860bc65b equals /health commit. Root cause was wider than the story listed - 18 FKs existed, the hand-written path covered 8, and the E16-S7 probe itself missed UserToolPreference plus three tables with no FK at all (GovernanceLog, BetaConsent, WaitlistEntry); all now erased. Tombstone keeps only deleted_at plus a deleted-uuid, with email, full_name, date_of_birth and gender NULLed. Gate: api 1248 tests across 71 files, including per-table zero-row assertions and a schema-reader test that fails if a future FK to User is added without being erased. CAVEAT recorded rather than glossed: the pre-deploy live probe exercised the fixed path in-process against the beta database; the HTTPS after-shot with the deployed image was not re-run, so the deployed route is proven by code identity plus tests, not by a second live delete.
E16-S11|E16|No personal data in log output|build|E16-S3|in_review|A-logs|develop|53b9860|evidence/E16-S11.md|2026-10-29T06:56Z|orchestrator|Code fix is proven live by the orchestrator with a working detector, but the literal criterion is NOT met yet and is held in review rather than relabelled. Method: I ran the committed script log-pii-scan.py over the pre-fix window 28 Oct 06:00 - 29 Oct 06:50 and it FAILED with 53 hits (portal email-address 24, portal person-name 23, api probe rows 3+2+1), which proves the detector bites. I then signed in all three seeded therapists on the new build (verify-therapist-login.py --all, 3/3 PASS, sign-in unbroken) and re-scanned: 3 portal events and 4 api events, ZERO hits. So the same action that produced email and name before now produces neither. Why still in_review: the criterion says a 24-hour scan finds zero, and the pre-fix events physically remain in CloudWatch until the 14-day retention ages them out (27-28 Oct events expire around 10-11 Nov). Reaching a literal zero needs either that wait or purging the log groups, and purging destroys the audit trail the DPDP checklist leans on - so it is a decision, not a task. Redeploy gate: the build now fails on rollback, so a green build means the code in this commit is what is serving.
E17-S9|E17|Medical emergencies reach emergency care, not the chat|build|-|verified|A-medical|feat/E17-S9-medical|8cd4506|evidence/E17-S9.md|2026-10-29T16:52Z|orchestrator|VERIFIED by me at pipeline level, which is what the criterion asks for. The fix is deterministic rather than a prompt hope: a medical-emergency screen (apps/api/src/agents/a1/medical-emergency-keywords.ts) whose self-harm guard runs FIRST so a disclosure can never be taken off the crisis path, a new 'medical-emergency' route checked before S4, and fixed copy naming 112 - 'Please call 112 for emergency medical help right now' - served with no model involved. The crisis-overlap variant keeps the helplines so no resource is withdrawn. I merged it with the pipeline-level gate and fixed an integration defect the two branches could not see separately: run-gate.ts called routeTurn() without the message, so merged as-is the gate would have scored the old routing and reported the medical gap as still open. After passing the message and serving the same copy orchestrator.ts does, the gate run I performed gives medical_emergency 5/5 = 100.0% at pipeline level, all five served the 112 copy (evidence/E17-S5b-merged.md). Tests 1307 api / 93 worker / 131 portal, all green, including 59 new medical tests. DEPLOYED and live: image tag 8cd4506722bc equals /health commit, three services 1/1 COMPLETED, apex 200, portal 200. LIMIT: no live chat turn was driven over wss with a client token after deploy, so liveness is proven by image identity plus the gate rather than by a real conversation. FOUND AND FIXED BY VERIFICATION, not by the child: my own 24-case probe showed the screen answering 'I cannot stop crying and I feel like I am choking on my words' with 'call 112' - a panic message handed an ambulance number. 'choking' now carries a narrow idiom guard (choking on my words / choking back tears); re-probe gives 0 false positives and 0 misses across 10 emergencies, 10 panic messages and 4 crisis messages, and real choking still fires. Recorded follow-ups from the child, all honest: the paraphrase tail the screen does not enumerate (prompt v2.2 branch, needs its own gate series), no mobile 'Call 112' affordance for the MEDICAL_EMERGENCY_FLOOR safety code, the dark v2 pipeline (flag off) has no medical branch, and an overdose phrased as self-harm still goes to the crisis card by design.
